From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msports: the COM port database

ComDBOpen, ComDBClose, ComDBGetCurrentPortUsage, ComDBClaimNextFreePort, ComDBClaimPort, ComDBReleasePort and ComDBResizeDatabase were spec stubs (UltiMaker Cura imports six). As the WDK describes the database: a bit per COM port number in the ComDB value of HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\COM Name Arbiter, 256 ports at least, grown by 1024 up to 4096, a named mutex around each access, read and written whole so every process sees the others' claims; a claimed port is claimed again only with ForceClaim (else ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION), no free port is ERROR_NO_LOG_SPACE, a size that is not a larger multiple of 1024 ERROR_BAD_LENGTH. Opening needs write access to the key (administrators). New msports.h.
